","ARTEMis is a key protein involved in DNA repair during V(D)R, which is essential for the proper functioning of the immune system. The V(D)R process is a process that occurs during the development of immune cells, such as neurons, where the DNA encoding the DNA-binding domains of the immune system proteins (e.g., the α- and β-chains of the dybrid β-galactosidase) is cleaved and re-liced to generate a mature protein. This process is essential for the proper functioning of the immune system, as it allows for the generation of a wide range of different immune cells that can recognize and kill a wide range of different pathogens.

