For the reactants:
2 moles of CO × 195.1 J/mol·K + 1 mole of O2 × 205.0 J/mol·K = 390.2 J/mol·K

Now, we can calculate the change in entropy:

ΔS = 427.4 J/mol·K - 390.2 J/mol·K = 37.2 J/mol·K

Since we have 3 moles of CO, we need to multiply the change in entropy by 3:

ΔS = 37.2 J/mol·K × 3 moles = 111.6 J/K

The change in entropy (ΔS) for the reaction is 111.6 J/K.

