","To prepare a selectively deuterium-labeled alkane from an alkene, you can use the following method:  
1. **Hydrodemetallation**: Treat the alkene with a deuterated borane (e.g., D₂BH₃) in the presence of a base (e.g., THF).  
2. **Reduction**: The deuterated borane (e.g., D₂BH₃) adds to the alkene to form a deuterated borane intermediate.  
3. **Deprotonation**: The base (e.g., THF) deprotonates the intermediate, leading to the formation of the deuterated alkane.  

This method is selective because the deuterated borane adds to the alkene in a syn fashion, resulting in the deuterium atom being added to the same side of the double bond.  

\boxed{\text{The deuterium is added to the same side of the double bond, resulting in a selective deuterium-labeled alkane.}}
