2. **Protein-protein interactions:** MBD2 interacts with other proteins, such as dememethylases (e.g., dememethyylase 10) and other methyltransferases, which can either promote or inhibit its dememethyation activity. These interactions can be influenced by the presence of other proteins, such as small-acting proteins (e.g., ubiquitin-like proteins) or post-translational modifications (e.g., phosphorylation).

