","The bond between nitrogen and oxygen in the molecule NO2 is polar. This is because nitrogen and oxygen have different electronegativities, which means they do not share the shared electrons equally in the bond. Oxygen is more electronegative than nitrogen, so it attracts the shared electrons more strongly, resulting in a partial negative charge on the oxygen atom and a partial positive charge on the nitrogen atom. This creates a polar bond.
