   \int_{-1}^{2} \left[(x^{2} + 3) - 1\right] \, dx = \int_{-1}^{2} (x^2 + 2) \, dx
   \]

2. **Integrate term by term:**  
   \[
   \int_{-1}^{2} (x^2 + 2) \, dx = \left[ \frac{x^3}{3} + 2x \right] \bigg|_{-1}^{2}
   \]

3. **Evaluate the definite integral:**  
   \[
   \left[ \frac{x^3}{3} + 2x \right] \bigg|_{-1}^{2} = \left( \frac{2^3}{3} + 2 \cdot 2 \right) - \left( \frac{-1^3}{3} + 2 \cdot (-1) \right)
   \]
