<start_of_turn>model
","1. **Calculate the total area of the courtyard**:  
   \[
   \text{Area} = \text{length} \times \text{width} = 50 \text{ m} \times 16.5 \text{ m} = 825 \text{ m}^2
   \]

2. **Calculate the area of one paving stone**:  
   \[
   \text{Area of one plate} = \text{length} \times \text{width} = 2.5 \text{ m} \times \text{width}
   \]

3. **Set up the equation**:  
   The total area of the carpet is equal to the number of plates multiplied by the area of one plate:  
   \[
   825 \text{ m}^2 = 165 \times (2.5 \text{ m} \times \text{width})
   \]

4. **Solve for the width**:  
   \[
   825 = 412.5 \times \text{width}
   \]
   \[
   \text{width} = \frac{825}{412.5} = 2 \text{ m}
   \]

   The width of each paving stone is \(\boxed{2 \text{ m}}\).
