","(a) $\int_{-1}^{1} 2^{x} d x = \frac{2^{x}}{\ln 2} \bigg]_{-1}^{1} = \frac{2^{1}}{\ln 2} - \frac{2^{-1}}{\ln 2} = \frac{2 - \frac{1}{2}}{\ln 2} = \frac{\frac{3}{2}}{\ln 2} = \frac{3}{2\ln 2}$  

(b) $\int_{0}^{1}\left(3 e^{x}+ 2 \sqrt{x}\right) d x = \left(3 e^{x} + \frac{4}{3} x^{3/2}\right) \bigg|_{0}^{1} = \left(3 e^{1} + \frac{4}{3} \right) - \left(3 e^{0} + \frac{4}{3} \cdot 0^{3/2}\right) = 3e + \frac{4}{3} - 3 = 3e - \frac{5}{3}$  

