   \[
   \sigma_{\text{max}} = \frac{M h}{I}
   \]  
   where \( I \) is the moment of inertia of the beam. For a rectangular beam, \( I = \frac{b h^3}{12} \). Substituting \( I \) and \( M \) into the stress equation:  
   \[
   \sigma_{\text{max}} = \frac{F(l - x) - \frac{3}{8} \frac{Fc\sigma_{\text{max}}}{lb\tau_{\text{max}}} \cdot x}{b h^3/12}
   \]  
