","When primary cosmic rays collide with the Earth's atmosphere, they undergo a series of interactions that transform them into secondary cosmic rays. These interactions are primarily governed by the energy of the primary cosmic ray and the composition of the atmosphere. The energy distribution and composition of secondary cosmic rays are significantly affected by these interactions.

