\]  
Thus, the magnitude of the acceleration is \(\boxed{3.99 \times 10^5 \, \text{m/s}^2}\).  

(b) To find the time \(t\) required for the proton to reach a speed \(v = 35,000 \, \text{m/s}\), we use the kinematic equation:  
\[
v = u + at,
\]  
where \(u = 0\) (since the proton starts from rest). Solving for \(t\):  
\[
t = \frac{v - u}{a} = \frac{35,000 \, \text{m/s}}{3.99 \times 10^5 \, \text{m/s}^2} = 0.0877 \, \text{s}.
\]  
Thus, the time required is \(\boxed{0.0877 \, \text{s}}\).
