","Encasing small electronic components in a glass-like material can help cool them by providing a thermal insulator. Glass has a low thermal conductivity, meaning it does not conduct heat well. This means that the heat generated by the components will be less likely to escape into the surrounding environment, which can help maintain a lower temperature for the components.

